    "fact_rationales": {
      "F14": "Elevated serum creatinine indicates impaired renal function, which can be seen in various renal disorders, including Posterior Urethral Valves and Bilateral Hydronephrosis.",
      "F16": "Bladder wall irregularity and thickening, bilateral ureteral dilation, and urinary retention are consistent with Posterior Urethral Valves and Prune Belly Syndrome, which both involve obstructive uropathy.",
      "F3": "Bilateral renal enlargement and hydronephrosis is more typical of obstructive uropathy, which is consistent with Posterior Urethral Valves and Bilateral Hydronephrosis.",
      "F4": "A markedly dilated fetal bladder is highly suggestive of Posterior Urethral Valves, which causes lower urinary tract obstruction."
    },
